; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Cardioid from Lines
; CATEGORY: Spirals & Curves
; LEVEL:    Intermediate
; TAGS:     cardioid, times table, envelope, modular arithmetic, animation
; SUMMARY:  Joins point k to point 2k round a circle and a heart-shaped cardioid appears; then the multiplier slowly grows.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   Put 200 points round a circle and number them 0 to 199. Join
;   every point k to the point 2 x k (going round again past 199).
;   The straight lines crowd together along a heart-shaped curve
;   called a cardioid. With 3 x k you get a nephroid (two lobes),
;   with 4 x k three lobes, and so on. The program starts at 2 and
;   slowly raises the multiplier, pausing at each whole number.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run and watch. Press Stop to end. Change POINTS for more or
;   fewer lines, or TOP for the largest multiplier.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * modular arithmetic: counting past the last point wraps round
;   * a curve that appears as the "envelope" of straight lines
;   * the multiplier does not have to be a whole number
;   * animation that slows down at interesting moments
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Freeze the picture at 2 and count how many points you need for
;     the heart to look smooth.
;   * Try a multiplier of 34 or 51 with 100 points. Can you explain it?
;   * Color each line by its length instead of by k.
; ============================================================

make "points 200
make "radius 270
make "top 10

; Where point number p (any real number) sits on the circle.
; Point 0 is at the left, like the usual times-table circle drawings.
to place :p
  localmake "angle 270 + 360 * :p / :points
  output list :radius * sin :angle :radius * cos :angle
end

to timestable :m
  clean
  setpencolor [70 70 90] setpensize 2
  penup setxy minus :radius 0 setheading 0 pendown
  repeat 120 [forward 2 * pi * :radius / 120 right 3]
  setpensize 1
  for [k 0 :points - 1] [
    ; colors run round the rainbow as k goes round the circle
    localmake "h 360 * :k / :points
    setpencolor (list 128 + 120 * sin :h 128 + 120 * sin :h + 120 128 + 120 * sin :h + 240)
    penup setpos place :k
    ; k x m may be bigger than the last point number, or a fraction.
    ; PLACE uses SIN and COS, which repeat every full turn, so point
    ; 250 lands where point 50 is: the wrapping round happens by itself.
    pendown setpos place :k * :m
  ]
  penup setxy -390 -290 setpencolor [200 200 200]
  label (sentence [multiplier] (round :m * 100) / 100)
end

clearscreen hideturtle
setbackground [15 15 25]
setlabelheight 16
make "m 2
forever [
  timestable :m
  ; linger on whole numbers, glide between them
  ifelse (abs :m - round :m) < 0.001 [wait 90] [wait 1]
  make "m :m + 0.02
  if :m > :top + 0.001 [make "m 2]
]
